Derived material:
  * The algorithms for PEP 440 version parsing and ordering, specifier
    matching (including the interval logic of packaging/_ranges.py),
    PEP 508 requirement and marker parsing and evaluation, and name and
    filename normalization are ports of the corresponding pypa/packaging
    modules to Kotlin.
  * The conformance test vectors in src/test/resources/pypa/ were
    extracted from pypa/packaging's tests/test_version.py,
    test_specifiers.py, test_requirements.py, test_markers.py and
    test_utils.py by tools/harvest_pypa_vectors.py, and the tests in
    src/test/kotlin/dev/greenflagged/pypackaging/conformance/ port the
    corresponding upstream test functions.

The Unicode tables in src/main/kotlin/dev/greenflagged/pypackaging/internal/
PyUnicodeTables.kt are generated from the Unicode Character Database as
exposed by CPython's unicodedata module. That data is used under the
Unicode License v3; its copyright and permission notice is in
LICENSE-UNICODE.

The test-only corpus in src/test/resources/pypi-corpus.json.gz consists of
version strings published on the Python Package Index, collected by
tools/pypi-corpus/collect.py. It is not part of the published jar.
